@startuml 02-lobby-commands-request
!include _common.puml
title 02 · Lobby commands — request (client → server) · Socket / RMI
autonumber

box "Client" #E3F2FD
participant UI as "Client UI\n(GUI / CLI)"
participant VS as "VirtualServer\n(Socket / RMI)"
end box

participant NET as "Network"

box "Server" #E8F5E9
participant EP as "SocketClientHandler /\nGameServerRemoteImpl\n(inbound dispatcher)"
participant LM as "LobbyManager\n(lobby-thread)"
end box

== User action ==
UI -> VS : sendCreateLobby(n) / sendJoinLobby(id) / sendListLobbies() / sendLeaveCommand()
note over VS : builds a LobbyCommand

== Transport to the server ==
alt Socket transport
  VS -> NET : send(cmd): synchronized(out) writeObject(cmd) + flush
  NET -> EP : ClientCommand
  EP -> EP : SocketClientHandler.run(): in.readObject(); cmd.accept(dispatcher)
else RMI transport
  VS -> NET : submitAsync(cmd): commandExecutor → serverStub.submitClientCommand(cmd)
  NET -> EP : submitClientCommand(cmd)
  EP -> EP : command.accept(dispatcher)
end

EP -> EP : dispatcher.visit(LobbyCommand)
EP -> LM : lobbyManager.submit(cmd)
note right of EP : lobby commands are enqueued,\nnot executed inline

== Processing on the lobby-thread ==
LM -> LM : queue.put(cmd) → run(): cmd.accept(this)

alt visit(CreateLobbyCommand)
  LM -> LM : guards: already in game / already in lobby / size in 2..5 ?
  LM -> LM : new Lobby(...); lobbies.put(id, lobby); lobby.addPlayer(entry)
else visit(JoinLobbyCommand)
  LM -> LM : guards: already in game/lobby; lobby exists & not full ?
  LM -> LM : lobby.addPlayer(entry); startIfFull(lobby)
  note right of LM : if the lobby fills up → game start (diagram 08)
else visit(ListLobbiesCommand)
  LM -> LM : getView(name).sendLobbyList(currentLobbyListDto())
else visit(LeaveCommand)
  LM -> LM : finished game → session queue; in lobby → handleLeaveFromLobby; else sendError
end

note over UI, LM
  All server → client responses (LobbyList / LobbyState / GameStarting / Error)
  are covered in diagram 03.
end note
@enduml
